---
// /privacy/: what this site counts and stores (DECISIONS D26). Each claim
// names the code that makes it true. Keep it true: when a claim stops
// holding, change the page in the same PR.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/paths';
---
<Base short="Privacy"
      description="What this site counts, what it saves in a visitor's browser, and which other sites a visitor's browser contacts.">
  <!-- Copy drafted with AI assistance; needs MCO staff review before launch (UM AI disclosure). -->
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>

    {/* No cookies: nothing in src/ sets document.cookie; GoatCounter sets
        none (src/scripts/analytics.ts). */}
    <p>This site sets no cookies, and it never asks anyone for personal information.</p>

    <h2>Page counts</h2>
    {/* src/scripts/analytics.ts: p, t, s, r (host only), q (utm_* only);
        skipped on Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control. */}
    <p>
      We count page views with <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/">GoatCounter</a>, the same
      counter the Station Dashboard uses. Each count records the page and its title, the visitor's
      screen size, the name of the site that linked to the page, and any campaign tags in the link.
      It records no cookie, name or account.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing is counted when a browser sends Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control.
    </p>

    <h2>What the browser keeps</h2>
    {/* MCO.initThemeToggle via src/scripts/chrome.ts: localStorage
        'mco-theme', shared with the Mesonet tools (HOUSE-STYLE §4). */}
    <p>
      When someone picks a theme, the site saves that choice in their browser, so the next page and
      the Mesonet tools open in the same theme. Clearing the browser's site data removes it.
    </p>

    <h2>Other sites a page contacts</h2>
    {/* src/kit/csp.ts lists every host a page may reach. */}
    <p>
      Pages load fonts and shared code from jsDelivr, and read station data and photos from our
      own servers. The homepage map loads its code from unpkg, its basemap from CARTO and its terrain
      from Amazon Web Services. The conditions card on the homepage reads the National Weather
      Service forecast for whichever station a visitor picks. Each of these services sees the
      visitor's IP address, as every website does.
    </p>

    <h2>Mesonet app</h2>
    <p>
      The Montana Mesonet app has its own <a href={url('mesonet/app/privacy/')}>privacy policy</a>.
      Questions go to <a href="mailto:state.climatologist@umontana.edu">state.climatologist@umontana.edu</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
